            <div xml:id="d224">

                <pb facs="0328" n="226" sameAs="frus:frus1933v03/pg226"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/6005: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China (Johnson) to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1933-03-09T09:00:00+08:00">March 9, 1933—9
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received March 9—12:20 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>226. Reuter reports from Nanking and Tokyo yesterday that both the Chinese
                    Government and the Manchukuo authorities have issued mandates depriving General
                    Tang Yu-lin, former chairman of Jehol of all his civil and military posts.
                    Nanking has also ordered his arrest and punishment for desertion.</p>
                <p>Manchukuo has appointed General Chang Hai-peng Governor of Jehol.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Johnson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
